member.summary:
Serialize an object as its runtime type (from ) rather than as , so serializers that add type information for polymorphic values don't do so for the root.

    SomeType data = new SomeType();
    Object obj = data;
    var a = serializer.Serialize(data);
    var b = serializer.Serialize(obj);
    var c = serializer.SerializeWithoutType(obj);

For the above, a and c will be equal, b may contain type information (depending on the serializer).

Serialize an object to text as its runtime type (from ) rather than as , so serializers that add type information for polymorphic values don't do so for the root.

    SomeType data = new SomeType();
    Object obj = data;
    var a = serializer.ToString(data);
    var b = serializer.ToString(obj);
    var c = serializer.ToStringWithoutType(obj);

For the above, a and c will be equal, b may contain type information (depending on the serializer).
